          "path": "_m/u/3/2/j/gorleben-wp/sc-405043-russian-boy-is-adopt.jpg",
          "filename": "SC 405043 - Russian boy is adopted by Co F., 175th Infantry, 29th Infantry Division, Ninth U.S. Army as their mascot. (52117092382).jpg",
          "caption": "His greatest enjoyment is searching S.S. troopers' rolls. Both of his parents were killed in Kiev, Russia[sic], and his ambition is to avenge his parents' death. Capt. Le Roy S. Stanley, C.O., made him honorary 1st Sergeant. Known to the men in his unit as Ivan, he has already earned his Good Conduct Medal. Uniform was made by army nurses. \nGorleben, Germany. 3 May, 1945.\nCo. F, 175th Inf., 29th Inf. Div. NUSA.\nPhotographer: T/5 Romeo E. Michaud, 3264.\n\nPhoto Source: U.S. National Archives. Digitized by Signal Corps Archive.",
